    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was founded as a shipping point for the Meramec Iron Works, which shipped its products by wagon train.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._James%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "James Chapel and Verkamp Shelter are listed on the National Register of Historic Places, preserving the town’s 19th‑century heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._James%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The James Memorial Library, a community hub, sits beside James City Park, offering residents a quiet place to read.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._James%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Saint James nestles in the foothills of the Ozark Mountains at 37°59′56″N 91°36′59″W, giving it a scenic hilltop feel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
